('G4019','grc','περιδέω','perideō','G:V','to wrap around','περι-δέω 
 [in LXX: Job.12:18 (אָסַר)* ;] 
to tie round, bind round: with accusative and dative, pass., Jhn.11:44.†
 (AS)'),
('G4020','grc','περιεργάζομαι','periergazomai','G:V','be a busybody','περι-εργάζομαι 
 [in LXX: Wis.8:5 א1, Sir.3:23 * ;] 
__1. to waste one''s labour about a thing. 
 __2. to be a busybody: 2Th.3:11 (cf. Plat., Apol., 19 B).†
 (AS)'),
('G4021','grc','περίεργος','periergos','G:A','meddlesome/magic','περίεργος, -ον 
 __I. of persons; 
 __1. over careful. 
 __2. curious, meddling, a busybody: 1Ti.5:13. 
 __II. Of things; 
 __1. over-wrought. 
 __2. super­fluous. 
 __3. curious, uncanny; τὰ π., curious arts, magic: Act.19:19 (see Deiss., BS, 3235.).†
 (AS)'),
('G4022','grc','περιέρχομαι','perierchomai','G:V','to go around','περι-έρχομαι 
 [in LXX chiefly for סָבַב ;] 
